  <section>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>Dexter is a small Penobscot County town of approximately 3,800 residents, situated between Bangor (45 min east) and Dover-Foxcroft (30 min north). The town sits at the junction of ME-7 and ME-94, and historically was a manufacturing and textile center anchored by the Dexter woolen mill complex. Today, the town's economy combines small-business retail, lakes-region recreation (Lake Wassookeag, Puffers Pond, Sebasticook River), and a steady commuter population that works in Bangor and the surrounding region.</p>
    <p>Dexter has one cannabis dispensary — Puffers Place, a medical operator that distinguishes itself with an on-site 420-friendly lakefront rental property on Puffers Pond. The combination of dispensary plus lodging is unusual among Maine medical operators and positions Puffers Place as a destination for cannabis-curious travelers seeking a multi-day Maine experience rather than a transactional purchase.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Puffers Place — Medical Dispensary</h2>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 50 Johnson Road, Dexter, ME 04930<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 270-1064<br>
    <strong>Hours:</strong> Mon-Thu 9am-7pm · Fri-Sat 9am-8pm · Sun 9am-5pm (per puffersplace.com)<br>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Medical (MMMP cardholders) — per Yelp and the operator's site<br></p>
    <p>Per Yelp and the operator's own site, Puffers Place operates as a medical cannabis dispensary with a full menu — premium medical marijuana strains, CBD topicals, smoking accessories, and online product ordering. Per Yelp, they also offer medical marijuana card services (provider referrals) for patients seeking certification.</p>
    <p>The operator's positioning is patient-focused and rural: small-town service, medical-grade product, and an on-site property for cannabis-curious visitors who want to extend their visit into a multi-day stay.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The Puffers Pond Lodge — 420-Friendly Lodging</h2>
    <p>Per the operator's site, Puffers Place operates a "cannabis-friendly seasonal rental home" on Puffers Pond — a lakefront property with kayaks, a private dock, and lake views. The Lodge is positioned for "families or small groups seeking rest, privacy, and relaxation in nature" with explicit 420-friendly accommodations.</p>
    <p>This combination — dispensary + on-site 420-friendly lodging — is rare in Maine's medical cannabis market. Most operators are retail-only. Puffers Place's lodging property adds a destination-stay element that draws visitors from outside the immediate Dexter area. For Maine cannabis tourists who want to combine dispensary shopping with a quiet lakefront stay, Puffers Place is one of the few operators offering both.</p>
    <p>Note: the lodging property is a separate booking from the dispensary. Confirm availability, rates, and any current policy updates directly with the operator.</p>
  </section>

